WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:06.049
Speaking of reelection, uh, there is something
very unusual happening in the democratic primary

00:00:06.049 --> 00:00:07.850
Republican turn Democrat.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:14.740
Michael Bloomberg is instantly polling 6%
in one recent poll and an average of 4% immediately

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.070
surpassing many candidates who have been in
this thing for six months, a year even longer.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.990
Uh, the new poll in which Michael Bloomberg
has polling 6% is from the Hill.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:28.790
Michael Bloomberg is of course the turbo billionaire
who is somewhere between 10 and 20 times richer

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.930
than our current billionaire president Donald
Trump.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.070
He has actually shaken up the race.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:39.410
If you look at the polling with Bloomberg
in the race, you see that in the polls in

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:46.199
which Bloomberg is included, there are currently
five being used to calculate Bloomberg's average

00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:47.829
of 4%.

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:53.249
You see that Joe Biden's support is mostly
unchanged, but both Elizabeth Warren and Bernie

00:00:53.249 --> 00:00:55.010
Sanders support is down.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.010
Tulsi.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.879
Gabbert has gone from polling one to three
in recent polls to polling just zero to two.

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:05.170
Camila Harris is polling as low as two once
you include Bloomberg, despite having been

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:10.250
as high as five or 6% in recent polls, there
are now discussions that Camilla Harris may

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.880
soon be exiting this race altogether.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.470
So let me get all the normal disclaimers out
of the way.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.270
I'm not supporting Michael Bloomberg.

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:22.240
I already got heat yesterday merely by pointing
out that Pete Buddha judge has been climbing

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.240
in the polls.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.900
People saying, David, you're a booted judge,
establishment shill.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.440
I'm not supporting Pete.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.970
I'm not supporting Michael Bloomberg.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.100
I'm simply telling you the numbers.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.470
Michael Bloomberg is very quickly having impact
that many candidates who have been in this

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:39.450
thing for six to 12 months have not been able
to make Deval.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.900
Patrick, when he got into the race, wanted
to make at least this level of impact has

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.580
failed to do so.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.920
And Michael Bloomberg is doing it to a degree
now.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.610
Can he make the debates?

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:56.570
On the one hand, Bloomberg has until December
12th to qualify on polling and donor numbers.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:02.410
Right now it is only Biden, Sanders, Warren,
Buddha, judge Harris and Clover char.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.650
There are six people in the next debate.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:08.890
If qualification closed today, Tom Stier would
be out.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:14.650
Tulsi Gabard would be out, Andrew Yang would
be out, Cory Booker and Julio on Castro would

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.050
not make the next debate.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.799
And of course, as of today, neither would
Bloomberg or Deval.

00:02:18.799 --> 00:02:23.590
Patrick Bloomberg may easily end up qualifying
on polling.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.670
The question is going to be donors, and I
actually don't know the answer to this.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.459
Bloomberg is not even accepting donations.

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:32.239
He's financing his own campaign.

00:02:32.239 --> 00:02:34.290
Can he even make the debate on that basis?

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:39.790
Since there is a donor requirement, he may
preclude himself from even maybe qualifying

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:40.889
because of that.

00:02:40.889 --> 00:02:43.319
Uh, he's been spending millions of dollars
on ads.

00:02:43.319 --> 00:02:47.769
Tons of our viewers have been telling me they're
regularly getting Michael Bloomberg ads before

00:02:47.769 --> 00:02:49.569
our videos on YouTube.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:53.040
The debate itself scheduled for December 19th.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.400
So what does this mean for Bloomberg?

00:02:55.400 --> 00:03:00.159
We have no polling from Iowa and New Hampshire,
Nevada or South Carolina, yet that includes

00:03:00.159 --> 00:03:06.870
Michael Bloomberg, 6% nationally or 4% nationally
is not going to mean much if he can't make

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.290
any headway in any of those first four primaries.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.829
I see Iowa as a very tough one for Michael
Bloomberg.

00:03:13.829 --> 00:03:16.040
New Hampshire is maybe more of a possibility.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:22.400
Nevada and South Carolina are certainly question
marks, but imagine being in this race for

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.250
months and months and then you see Bloomberg
enter and now you're instantly losing to him.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:34.609
Like if I were working for Camila Harris or
Andrew Yang, Amy Klobuchar, a Corey Booker

00:03:34.609 --> 00:03:42.230
Tulsi Gabard Julio on Castro, you just can't
seem to get past one to 3% in Harris's case.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:47.480
She actually was up to 11 or 12% at one point,
but has just fallen apart and then you see

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:53.540
Michael Bloomberg come in and he's averaging
4% and getting 6% in one poll.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.400
I would be extremely demoralized if I were
the candidates, if I were working on their

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.400
campaigns.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.090
I don't work on political campaigns, but that,
that's my sense of it.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.090
No doubt.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.669
This is going to hugely encourage Michael
Bloomberg.

00:04:05.669 --> 00:04:07.889
If he makes that next debate.

00:04:07.889 --> 00:04:12.739
I wouldn't be surprised to see him get quite
a bit of FaceTime merely for being able to

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:16.629
get this level of support in just a few weeks
after announcing.

00:04:16.629 --> 00:04:20.859
This does not, by the way, seemed like a particularly
fun time to be an Elizabeth Warren supporter.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:25.940
She has been in freefall, as I told you yesterday
for several weeks now with Michael Bloomberg

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:27.449
in and climbing.

00:04:27.449 --> 00:04:28.610
I can't imagine.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.590
This is what Elizabeth Warren and her supporters
want to see.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:34.410
Where will we be two weeks from now?

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.590
No idea.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:36.729
Absolutely no idea.

00:04:36.729 --> 00:04:42.340
This is a primary that is very quickly taking
on some different dynamics to say the least.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.759
And I wouldn't be surprised if, uh, everything
reverses in the next two weeks and we simply

00:04:46.759 --> 00:04:54.840
see a Warren Bernie Biden recover and be very
clearly the only people in front runner status.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.069
Or we may see Buddha judge continue to climb.

00:04:57.069 --> 00:04:59.319
We may see Michael Bloomberg get more traction.

00:04:59.319 --> 00:05:00.390
I have no idea.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:04.500
And of course for Michael Bloomberg, the possibility
of making that next debate, if indeed it is

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.800
even a possibility, given that he is financing
his own campaign will be a big factor in how

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:10.070
this thing plays out.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.070
Let me know what you think.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:16.039
We'll have a poll on our Instagram page about
this at David Pakman show.

00:05:16.039 --> 00:05:17.621
And while you're there, follow me.

00:05:17.621 --> 00:05:22.729
Me on Instagram as well@davidgotpackagedthedavidpakmanshowatdavidpakman.com

